# Miskatonic County Registrar's Office / Town Records.
# The bureaucratic apparatus: reasonable men executing an absence.
NPC: county_clerk
LOCATION: town_hall
SCHEDULE: morning=registrar, midday=registrar, evening=closed, night=closed

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(county_clerk, default) AND coat = plain
  TAG: clerk_plain
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v2
  MR. PENCE: "Public inspection hours end at four."
  [He moistens a fingertip on a porcelain sponge tray and turns a ledger leaf.]
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. PENCE: "If this is genealogical, the fee is twenty cents per volume.\nIf this is municipal, state the parcel."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(county_clerk, default)
  TAG: clerk_badge
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v2
  MR. PENCE: "Officer Corwin. Captain Odell sent over the preliminary notices this morning."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Did he send the full list?"
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v2
  MR. PENCE: "He sent six notices of sudden decease for probate indexing.\nThe forms are standard."

TOPIC: wage_claim_inquiry
  GATE: evidence(lay_lead) AND evidence(new_bedford_letters) AND evidence(postal_bureaucracy_refusal)
  TAG: clerk_wage_claim
  LABEL: "Attempt to file Naomi Freeman's wage claim"
  TIME: 10
  WALTER CORWIN: "I want to record an unpaid whaler's lay. Naomi Freeman, on behalf of an ancestor aboard the Ophion."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v2
  MR. PENCE: "You'd need a living claimant. A next of kin with legal standing."
  WALTER CORWIN: "The mother is dead. The boy found with her is dead."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v2
  MR. PENCE: "Then the claim abates. An estate requires an administrator appointed by probate, and Judge Wexford's seat is vacant, as you know."
  WALTER CORWIN: "There is an older son. Grown, and gone off on his own account. Surviving."
  VOICE: trombone_questioning_short_v1
  MR. PENCE: "Where does he reside?"
  WALTER CORWIN: "Whereabouts unknown. New Bedford, originally."
  [Mr. Pence sets his dry pen into the brass stand without looking up.]
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_long_v1
  MR. PENCE: "Then you have brought me no claimant at all, Officer.\nA man who cannot be served notice cannot tender his affidavit, and this office does not advertise in the wilderness."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. PENCE: "Produce the son in person with proof of identity, or the claim has no one to belong to."
  FORK:
    CHOICE: "Ask what becomes of a debt when the heir cannot be found."
      WALTER CORWIN: "So a debt simply evaporates because the surviving heir has gone out into the world?"
      VOICE: trombone_neutral_long_v2
      MR. PENCE: "It does not evaporate, Corwin. It abates.\nA claimant must appear to stand for himself. Until he signs the docket in ink, that is the nature of the statute, not a flaw in it."
      NOTEBOOK: clerk_claim_minor | "Registrar: a wage claim requires a living claimant able to appear and stand for himself. Naomi's surviving son is grown and gone on his own account with whereabouts unknown; the claim has no one to stand for it."
      EVIDENCE: claim_no_claimant
    CHOICE: "Insist on filing in triplicate under police authority."
      WALTER CORWIN: "Enter the claim in triplicate under my name as reporting officer, to preserve the record until the son comes forward."
      [Mr. Pence looks up over wire spectacles, pen poised.]
      VOICE: trombone_alarmed_long_v1
      MR. PENCE: "I will stamp it as received correspondence, Officer.\nIt sits in the dead-records drawer. It creates no lien, and twenty years from now nobody will look in that drawer."
      NOTEBOOK: clerk_claim_triplicate | "Wage claim submitted in triplicate as police correspondence to preserve the record for Naomi's surviving grown son, whose whereabouts are unknown; filed inertly in county dead-records drawer."
      EVIDENCE: claim_filed_inert

TOPIC: ophion_settlement
  GATE: evidence(behan_name) OR evidence(ophion_myth_classical)
  TAG: clerk_ophion_records
  LABEL: "Request the 1820s Ophion insurance and probate filings"
  TIME: 5
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. PENCE: "Volume 14, Maritime Disbursements and Marine Underwriting, 1823–1828."
  [He pulls a heavy sheepskin-bound folio with flaking spine.]
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v2
  MR. PENCE: "Underwriters' draft paid out to Pruitt, Corliss, and Wexford syndicates. Eighty-four thousand dollars in gold specie."
  WALTER CORWIN: "And the crew's families?"
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. PENCE: "Noted as 'Lost at sea; accounts closed by total abandonment.' No lay shares were distributed."
  WALTER CORWIN: "The same families bought the harbor mills eighteen months later."
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v1
  MR. PENCE: "The ledger notes transactions, Officer. It does not pass moral judgments on timing."
  NOTEBOOK: clerk_ophion_1 | "1820s probate records: $84,000 insurance paid to Pruitt/Corliss/Wexford syndicates. Crew accounts closed as total loss; zero lays paid."
  EVIDENCE: insurance_fraud_record

TOPIC: sixth_member_deed
# PERMANENT EXCLUSION — do not gate this live, see Design Law 5
  GATE: never
  #evidence(sixth_member) AND NOT topic_done(county_clerk, sixth_member_deed)
  TAG: clerk_sixth_man
  LABEL: "Check deeds and tax rolls for the Ophion Club property"
  TIME: 5
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. PENCE: "The estate deed is held in trust. Six shares of tenancy in common."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Name the shareholders."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. PENCE: "Absalom Wexford. Aldous Fenn. Miles Corliss. Josiah Pruitt. Otto Kessler."
  WALTER CORWIN: "That is five."
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v1
  MR. PENCE: "The sixth share is recorded simply as 'The Overseer of the Line.' No individual surname registered since the 1850 re-charter."
  WALTER CORWIN: "How does an unnameable title pay property tax?"
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v2
  MR. PENCE: "The check arrives drawn on the Boston Marine Bank. It clears. The county does not return legal currency."
  NOTEBOOK: clerk_sixth_man_1 | "The sixth Ophion Club share is deeded to 'The Overseer of the Line' without personal name; taxes paid via Boston Marine Bank."
  EVIDENCE: overseer_deed

# Shared inquiry: four different completed refusals make the question travel.
TOPIC: crew_omission
  GATE: topic_done(local_historian, crew_omission_official) AND NOT topic_done(county_clerk, crew_omission)
  TAG: county_clerk_crew_omission
  LABEL: "Ask why the town's history leaves out the crew's names"
  TIME: 3
  WALTER CORWIN: "Why does the town's history leave out the crew's names?"
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v1
  MR. PENCE: "Crew names belong in a shipping list, Officer. This is a county office."
  WALTER CORWIN: "I asked why the town's account leaves them out."
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v1
  MR. PENCE: "Then ask whoever composed the account. I certify records. I do not improve them."
  NOTEBOOK: crew_omission_refusal | "Asked Mr. Pence why the crew's names are missing from the town's history. No explanation supplied; the question remains open."
